    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "but what if they didn't use the community? if someone had the resources to build it in total isolation and then just \"released\" it through a shell company or a VC-backed group to gain instant legitimacy? i'm asking because i've seen parts of the core logic that i know for a fact i wrote under a different handle years ago, and it's like they just took my entire architecture and slapped their names on it. how would i even prove i'm the one who actually designed the consensus mechanism if the commit history is all managed by their \"team\"?",
